  "details": "1. In VRC tracking settings, enable `Display Eyetracking Debug` as well as `Force Eyetracking Raycast`.\n\n2. Look at a friend while their humanoid avatar is standing upright. Looks correct.\n\n3. Now ask them to sit/crouch down using an animation or playspace mover.\n\n4. Collider is now above the head, around where the nameplate is. Looking at the person, there's no raycast collision and we're focusing on the wall behind them.\n\nThe same happens when they move up with the playspace mover, the head ends up above the ray collider.\n\nIf I were to guess, the raycast is done too early in the frame?",
